.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0 WITH LLVM-exception
.Dd November 20, 2026
.Dt NOQTIS-EXPIRE 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm noqtis-expire
.Nd say until when a seal key seals
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm noqtis expire
.Fl k Ar key
.Op Fl p Ar key.pub
.Fl -at Ar time
.Op Fl -reason Ar text
.Op Fl o Ar file
.Op Fl f
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm noqtis expire
writes a key statement
.Pq Ql noqtis-keys-1 , Xr noqtis-capsule 5 ,
signed by
.Ar key ,
that it seals until
.Ar time
and not after.
.Xr noqtis-check 1
.Fl -keys Ar file
then accepts a capsule sealed with
.Ar key
as it does without the statement until
.Ar time
has come.
From then on it accepts one only when a verified timestamp
.Pq Fl -anchor
shows that it was sealed before
.Ar time ,
as for a key revoked then
.Pq Xr noqtis-revoke 1 :
the manifest's
.Ql created
is the sealer's own word.
The time that has come is the clock of the computer that checks, or
.Ev SOURCE_DATE_EPOCH
when it is set.
.Pp
A key holds one statement: one that expires cannot also be rotated or
revoked by a second statement given with it.
To end a key early, give the revocation or the rotation in place of the
expiry.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl k Ar key , Fl -key Ns = Ns Ar key
The secret key that expires.
.It Fl p Ar key.pub , Fl -pub Ns = Ns Ar key.pub
Its public key.
Default:
.Ar key Ns Pa .pub .
.It Fl -at Ar time
When the key expires, as
.Ql YYYY-MM-DDTHH:MM:SSZ
(UTC, 1970 or later).
Required.
.It Fl -reason Ar text
Up to 255 bytes of text, kept in the statement.
.It Fl o Ar file , Fl -out Ns = Ns Ar file
Write the statement to
.Ar file
instead of standard output (also for
.Ar - ) .
.It Fl f , Fl -force
Replace
.Ar file
if it exists.
.El
.Pp
The secret key must not be under a passphrase: this command takes no
.Fl -pass-fd
or
.Fl -pass-env ,
so remove the passphrase first
.Pq Xr noqtis-passwd 1 Fl -no-pass
and put it back after.
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Bl -tag -width 3n -compact
.It 0
The statement was written.
.It 2
A usage error, a key file that cannot be read, a key that is not a
post-quantum signature key pair, or a file that cannot be written.
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ noqtis expire -k me --at 2028-01-01T00:00:00Z -o me.expires
$ noqtis check -p me.pub --keys me.expires results
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr noqtis 1 ,
.Xr noqtis-check 1 ,
.Xr noqtis-revoke 1 ,
.Xr noqtis-rotate 1 ,
.Xr nqkstmt 3 ,
.Xr noqtis-capsule 5
